            <div xml:id="d1280">

                <pb facs="1261" n="1251" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/4–2649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-26T17:00:00+08:00">April 26, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 26—9:30 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1368. Neither Admiral Badger nor I have ordered anyone leave Shanghai. Mr.
                    Flanley spoke to ITT referring to final warning issued by ConGen (ConGentel
                    1342, April 25) and to telephone conversation re key Telephone Co. personnel
                    whom we agreed last December to evacuate in final evacuation if they so
                    desired.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
